# Security and limits

## Secrets

- Gemini / third-party API keys — server-side only (Edge Function env)
- Supabase `service_role` — never in Vue or client `.env`
- Client gets anon key + RLS only

## Data

- RLS on every user-specific table: a user sees only their rows
- Validate on the client (Regle) and never trust the client in Edge Functions
- Do not surface internal backend errors to the user
- Do not collect extra personal data

## External APIs — thrift and fallback

Before any request: limit / cooldown / cache → otherwise show "Try again later".

| Service | Client | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| Open Food Facts | debounce 500–800 ms, min 2–3 chars, staleTime, pagination | manual calorie/macro entry |
| Gemini | Analyze button only, compression, cooldown | app works without AI |
| TheMealDB | cache, no repeat fetches | Recommendations unavailable, Dashboard stays up |

Never call AI automatically on page load.

## Photos

Check MIME and size → compress / downscale → send. Cap upload size. Do not keep photos in Storage after AI processing unless the user saves them.

## Edge Function

Verify auth, validate input, rate-limit per user, return a structured result (calories only), do not leak the raw Gemini response.
